1
00:00:00,058 --> 00:00:01,480
This past year…

2
00:00:01,973 --> 00:00:04,960
There were stories that brought happiness.

3
00:00:05,088 --> 00:00:06,200
And there were stories that…

4
00:00:06,853 --> 00:00:08,213
that were sad to me.

5
00:00:08,474 --> 00:00:11,739
And something that I thought I should have done better.

6
00:00:11,862 --> 00:00:14,960
Especially, when I felt burnt out.

7
00:00:15,131 --> 00:00:19,000
I couldn't do it anymore. We talked and I felt so exhausted.

8
00:00:19,803 --> 00:00:22,240
Do you know what I did when I felt so exhausted?

9
00:00:22,358 --> 00:00:24,300
I read letters from my fans.

10
00:00:24,411 --> 00:00:26,080
I don't have a lot of friends.

11
00:00:26,155 --> 00:00:29,880
I don't share my life with so many people but I share it with Ling.

12
00:00:30,038 --> 00:00:36,080
This path iwasn't easy for me. It took time.

13
00:00:36,176 --> 00:00:38,440
I think if I asked Orm about it.

14
00:00:38,592 --> 00:00:41,240
She would say that I wasn't that friendly.

15
00:00:41,360 --> 00:00:43,241
When I watched myself being around Ling

16
00:00:43,261 --> 00:00:45,960
I asked myself 'why did she love me so much?'

17
00:00:46,760 --> 00:00:51,440
I understand why our fans like to see us together.

18
00:00:51,561 --> 00:00:53,000
(In unison) One..two…three.

19
00:00:53,067 --> 00:00:55,184
- Ta-da... - I've never seen this one.

20
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:05,440
Hello. I am Jo Paran Chiamchittrong.

21
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:06,500
This is Dear Myself,

22
00:01:06,522 --> 00:01:08,240
a deep conversation to warm your heart.

23
00:01:08,250 --> 00:01:11,240
We invite our guests to tell their stories through their photos.

24
00:01:11,400 --> 00:01:14,120
Our guests today are LingOrm. Hello.

25
00:01:14,401 --> 00:01:16,280
(In unison) Hello, hello.

26
00:01:16,502 --> 00:01:19,960
I'm so glad to see both of you again.

27
00:01:20,062 --> 00:01:21,063
From our last conversation,

28
00:01:21,073 --> 00:01:23,902
You said that your lives after your first series were fast-forward.

29
00:01:24,136 --> 00:01:27,944
I followed your stories for one year and a half

30
00:01:28,074 --> 00:01:29,920
and they were even faster than pushing a fast-forward button.

31
00:01:30,275 --> 00:01:31,276
So fast.

32
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:35,360
- Fast-forward button? - I totally forgot that this younger generation don't know about it.

33
00:01:35,374 --> 00:01:37,200
- I know what it is. - You do?

34
00:01:37,448 --> 00:01:39,039
I know. I know what it is.

35
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:41,761
- Your lives are moving so fast, are you? - You're right.

36
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:45,520
It was so fast that I felt like…

37
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:50,080
I didn't remember much even if I focused on it.

38
00:01:50,259 --> 00:01:54,595
- I didn't even have time to let it sink in. - I see.

39
00:01:55,485 --> 00:01:57,240
I need to give myself a little more time.

40
00:01:57,432 --> 00:01:59,120
What about you, Orm?

41
00:01:59,843 --> 00:02:04,120
Like I said everything happened rapidly because I'd forget everything.

42
00:02:04,184 --> 00:02:05,678
I mean like I don't ….

43
00:02:06,003 --> 00:02:09,759
I mean I don't normally pay attention at the calendar.

44
00:02:09,943 --> 00:02:13,200
I focus on my work, day by day. I don't even know what date was.

45
00:02:13,608 --> 00:02:15,800
Then I would be like…

46
00:02:16,088 --> 00:02:18,300
Oh! It's Ling's birthday!' Like I forgot it.

47
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:21,440
When time is moving rapidly, we'd like to bring you back in time.

48
00:02:21,886 --> 00:02:24,160
I gave you questions about photos.

49
00:02:24,259 --> 00:02:27,200
We will recap your lives through photos.

50
00:02:27,576 --> 00:02:29,920
I guess your life is stored in your phone.

51
00:02:30,163 --> 00:02:32,164
- Your photos are mostly in your phone. - That's right.

52
00:02:32,534 --> 00:02:35,280
- The first question is… - It is…

53
00:02:35,312 --> 00:02:39,000
The first LingOrm photo that you've kept in your phone.

54
00:02:39,040 --> 00:02:40,800
- Did you see each other's photos yet? - Not yet.

55
00:02:40,853 --> 00:02:43,091
I don't think so.

56
00:02:43,176 --> 00:02:47,543
- Ling, what is your first photo? - [First airdropped photo from costume fitting.]

57
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:52,079
This is the first photo of your question.

58
00:02:52,100 --> 00:02:54,600
It wasn't taken from my phone but

59
00:02:54,904 --> 00:02:58,280
it was taken during costume fitting of The Secret of Us.

60
00:02:58,323 --> 00:03:00,920
I like this one in particular

61
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:04,400
so I asked them to airdrop it for meright on the spot.

62
00:03:04,679 --> 00:03:07,280
I think our fans saw it already.

63
00:03:07,336 --> 00:03:11,360
Earn and Fahlada, both in grey outfits, hugged each other.

64
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:14,320
Their noses almost touched.

65
00:03:14,547 --> 00:03:16,520
- This is my first photo. - What did your caption say?

66
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:20,400
I wrote 'first airdropped photo from costume fitting.'

67
00:03:20,591 --> 00:03:23,640
When you looked at the photo, what came to your mind?

68
00:03:23,670 --> 00:03:25,671
I wondered why this photo popped up

69
00:03:26,780 --> 00:03:28,120
as our very first ones taken together.

70
00:03:28,326 --> 00:03:32,760
I thought the first photo should be a selfie type.

71
00:03:33,355 --> 00:03:34,800
When I thought about it

72
00:03:35,296 --> 00:03:39,840
actually I looked through the screen and I liked it a lot.

73
00:03:40,331 --> 00:03:43,317
so I asked them to airdrop it for meright on the spot.

74
00:03:43,451 --> 00:03:45,760
This was the first thought that came to my mind.

75
00:03:46,086 --> 00:03:50,280
Our three series gave different vibes.

76
00:03:50,507 --> 00:03:53,960
For me, I feel like this series

77
00:03:54,597 --> 00:03:57,220
gave me puppy love vibe.

78
00:03:57,403 --> 00:04:00,200
What's on your mind when you see this photo?

79
00:04:00,347 --> 00:04:03,560
- I can feel the innocent vibe. - It's not just the innocent vibe in the series.

80
00:04:03,803 --> 00:04:06,960
- We both were so innocent back then. - Fresh and innocent.

81
00:04:07,011 --> 00:04:11,200
I looked at our photos when we first worked together,

82
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:14,640
and I thought that our eyes were so bright and shiny.

83
00:04:14,676 --> 00:04:19,862
- Like we still had enough sleep. - That's right, we used to discuss about that.

84
00:04:19,899 --> 00:04:23,360
I feel like I'm a completely third wheel.

85
00:04:23,414 --> 00:04:26,600
You were gigling together and I'm the third wheel.

86
00:04:26,694 --> 00:04:31,960
It was fun for us, we don't normally sit down and talk like this together.

87
00:04:32,216 --> 00:04:36,080
It's nice because we have a chance to have deep conversation too.

88
00:04:37,520 --> 00:04:40,259
What did you see in the photo? It was back in 2024.

89
00:04:40,318 --> 00:04:42,800
- It wasn't that long ago. - Not long at all.

90
00:04:43,176 --> 00:04:45,760
Actually, our very first photos together

91
00:04:45,998 --> 00:04:49,520
should be around when we went to acting class.

92
00:04:49,768 --> 00:04:54,769
I got a new phone so it was our first photo together for me.

93
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:57,001
- I see, you went to an acting class together? - That's right.

94
00:04:57,222 --> 00:04:59,520
- We were so innocent looking. - I know.

95
00:05:00,496 --> 00:05:03,400
We were so excited for our costume fitting.

96
00:05:03,497 --> 00:05:05,920
Right now, it wasn't that excited for us anymore.

97
00:05:05,947 --> 00:05:09,720
I mean it was fun for me but it's not that excited anymore.

98
00:05:09,803 --> 00:05:12,804
- You kind of get used to it, you can expect what you will get. - That's right.

99
00:05:15,136 --> 00:05:19,080
Let's see your photo, Orm? What's the first one in your phone.

100
00:05:19,232 --> 00:05:22,280
I know about this one.

101
00:05:22,384 --> 00:05:27,080
Who took this one for you? Mom?

102
00:05:28,102 --> 00:05:30,682
No, one of the actresses took it.

103
00:05:30,731 --> 00:05:34,920
Right! Was it Ice? Ice took it for us.

104
00:05:34,998 --> 00:05:38,960
I think it was first time that we worked together.

105
00:05:39,547 --> 00:05:43,800
To model Thai traditional outfits for one of the designers.

106
00:05:45,766 --> 00:05:50,362
I remember that there were so many actors and actresses.

107
00:05:51,611 --> 00:05:53,400
We were there since early morning.

108
00:05:53,718 --> 00:05:56,960
I didn't have any friends, except Ling.

109
00:05:57,099 --> 00:05:59,200
- You sounded so sad. - But I just got…

110
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:03,960
I got to meet Ling late afternoon, after getting makeup done.

111
00:06:04,203 --> 00:06:06,880
It was bit lonely but I got Ling. And we chatted...

112
00:06:07,286 --> 00:06:10,240
Did we talk about our company?

113
00:06:10,283 --> 00:06:15,280
We talked. I knew that you would audition for the role.

114
00:06:15,323 --> 00:06:19,560
- You were about to audition. - Really? I wasn't sure if Ling who would join me.

115
00:06:19,814 --> 00:06:23,600
- But I didn't tell Orm about it. - Oh, you kept a secret from her.

116
00:06:23,608 --> 00:06:25,440
- Ling kept a secret from you? - That's right.

117
00:06:25,450 --> 00:06:28,720
I asked her like 'hey, it looked like we'd be in a series together,'

118
00:06:28,751 --> 00:06:30,000
or something like that.

119
00:06:30,056 --> 00:06:33,280
- That was your conversation that day? - If I didn't mix it up, I think so.

120
00:06:33,296 --> 00:06:36,120
Are we going to be in the series together?' 'What's it about?'

121
00:06:36,197 --> 00:06:38,480
Well, I don't know either', something like that.

122
00:06:39,198 --> 00:06:42,159
And I was like 'let's take a picture together.'

123
00:06:42,758 --> 00:06:48,320
- This photo was way back… - Even before the casting process.

124
00:06:48,582 --> 00:06:52,440
If you could talk to a person in that photo, what'd you say?

125
00:06:52,643 --> 00:06:57,500
Keep going! Congrats! Your life will be completely different after this.

126
00:06:58,190 --> 00:06:59,960
- What about you, Ling? - Me?

127
00:07:00,206 --> 00:07:02,320
I'm glad we got to work together.

128
00:07:02,686 --> 00:07:03,687
Aww.

129
00:07:05,470 --> 00:07:08,840
- You two have been stuck together until now. - That's right.

130
00:07:09,176 --> 00:07:11,247
Who'd have thought that we'd be together every day after that.

131
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:13,800
I remember from our last conversation

132
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:17,800
it started with a food truck for only 40-50 people.

133
00:07:17,811 --> 00:07:19,680
- That's right. - One food truck.

134
00:07:19,700 --> 00:07:23,920
I still got that photo, I looked through my phone.

135
00:07:23,940 --> 00:07:25,640
Then it became a fan meeting for 2,000 people.

136
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:28,760
After that, you booked Impact Arena, and you went to fashion week.

137
00:07:28,886 --> 00:07:30,160
- That's right. - Wow!

138
00:07:30,387 --> 00:07:34,560
Two ladies in the photo had no idea that they'd come this far.

139
00:07:34,880 --> 00:07:38,120
No way. I didn't expect that in my head.

140
00:07:38,238 --> 00:07:43,390
- Look at her, she looked so pretty in this. - I wore Thai traditional outfit.

141
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:44,600
So pretty.

142
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:49,640
- Let's look at the second question. - Let's go.

143
00:07:49,736 --> 00:07:53,327
A photo with the most memorable moment in the past year.

144
00:07:53,462 --> 00:07:57,600
I can guess your most memorable moment of the two of you.

145
00:07:57,760 --> 00:07:59,161
Ling, what is your photo?

146
00:07:59,560 --> 00:08:01,840
I sent in a photo that…

147
00:08:02,182 --> 00:08:06,920
It was our first fancon, we took it with our fans when we were on stage.

148
00:08:07,424 --> 00:08:11,200
There were 12,000 people.

149
00:08:11,627 --> 00:08:13,040
- I see. - That's right.

150
00:08:14,841 --> 00:08:19,600
I wrote 'I've never thought that this picture would happen in my life.'

151
00:08:19,712 --> 00:08:23,680
What is on your mind right now when you thought of that day?

152
00:08:23,982 --> 00:08:27,534
- Like picture? - Or your feeling back then.

153
00:08:27,651 --> 00:08:30,520
My first feeling was that…

154
00:08:31,318 --> 00:08:32,519
I didn't want to do it.

155
00:08:32,798 --> 00:08:33,799
That's right.

156
00:08:34,595 --> 00:08:35,596
Is it weird?

157
00:08:35,774 --> 00:08:39,520
I'm not a good singer, and I don't like to perform.

158
00:08:39,619 --> 00:08:41,200
I didn't know how to dance.

159
00:08:41,443 --> 00:08:45,600
- The things that I had to do on stage… - Sing and dance.

160
00:08:45,694 --> 00:08:48,640
I had to dance and sing.

161
00:08:48,846 --> 00:08:55,400
When I stepped into the project,

162
00:08:57,451 --> 00:09:01,640
my thought started to change along the way.

163
00:09:03,120 --> 00:09:05,760
I felt like I needed to do my best.

164
00:09:05,886 --> 00:09:07,480
I wanted it to be the best that I could.

165
00:09:07,512 --> 00:09:11,680
My 12,000 fans came from different places

166
00:09:11,755 --> 00:09:14,280
and they deserved to be happy.

167
00:09:14,424 --> 00:09:19,000
There were so many people working back office for our project

168
00:09:19,163 --> 00:09:21,800
with the fans. And I felt that I should…

169
00:09:22,352 --> 00:09:25,000
do my best so that everyone

170
00:09:25,875 --> 00:09:30,240
would be happy and it should be worth their hard work.

171
00:09:31,502 --> 00:09:34,100
There were 12,000 people and it was hard to pull it off.

172
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:38,760
It was so hard. The fans came from different places.

173
00:09:41,853 --> 00:09:45,120
It was so amazing.

174
00:09:45,470 --> 00:09:47,700
It was so valuable to me.

175
00:09:48,014 --> 00:09:52,600
I didn't think that this would happen to me either.

176
00:09:53,443 --> 00:09:56,920
I could do it all but I wasn't good at it.

177
00:09:57,144 --> 00:10:00,040
Really? Cause I thought you did it well.

178
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:06,480
I know the level of my competency in each thing I do.

179
00:10:06,667 --> 00:10:09,216
I thought that I wasn't good a professional back then

180
00:10:09,303 --> 00:10:11,241
I could memorize it but for a short period of time.

181
00:10:11,488 --> 00:10:14,040
Ling would memorize the dance routines

182
00:10:14,059 --> 00:10:16,294
- That's right. - and I would teach Ling.

183
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:18,800
Ling couldn't dance well but she was good at memorizing the routines.

184
00:10:18,961 --> 00:10:21,088
I was bad at memorizing but I could dance.

185
00:10:21,371 --> 00:10:25,640
We needed to work together.

186
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:29,280
Ling would be like 'Orn, the next move was like this'.

187
00:10:29,443 --> 00:10:31,680
But she didn't remember what was next. And I'd be like 'I know.'

188
00:10:32,152 --> 00:10:34,640
It was this move, you know what I mean?

189
00:10:35,203 --> 00:10:39,840
I'm not good at memorizing so I would be stressed out about this.

190
00:10:40,270 --> 00:10:42,882
- But Orm, you sent the same photo in. - That's right.

191
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:46,440
- I just saw it. - It leads to the next photo and it was so funny.

192
00:10:46,744 --> 00:10:49,240
You chose the photo of our front but I chose the one with our back.

193
00:10:49,294 --> 00:10:51,600
You two chose same photo but from different angle.

194
00:10:52,805 --> 00:10:56,600
I wrote 'Love you all, I'm so proud of us.'

195
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:59,280
By 'us' I didn't mean just Ling and I,

196
00:10:59,648 --> 00:11:00,760
but I mean all of us.

197
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:04,040
I've never thought that my life would have come this far.

198
00:11:04,526 --> 00:11:06,360
It's a photo that made me feel

199
00:11:07,443 --> 00:11:09,520
like I needed to remember

200
00:11:10,780 --> 00:11:13,640
how good we all were.

201
00:11:13,832 --> 00:11:17,400
We are right here at this spot.

202
00:11:17,934 --> 00:11:20,160
Everyone supported us until we're standing right here.

203
00:11:20,264 --> 00:11:22,600
If we were missing just one person,

204
00:11:23,632 --> 00:11:24,920
it wouldn't turn out to be like this.

205
00:11:25,211 --> 00:11:27,760
On our bad days,

206
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:31,500
it happened sometimes on internet

207
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:33,520
or the real world that I felt like

208
00:11:33,982 --> 00:11:36,360
this argument was unreasonable or I didn't know

209
00:11:36,547 --> 00:11:39,240
why people were mad at us. I wanted to remember

210
00:11:39,555 --> 00:11:41,035
that they were just a small part.

211
00:11:41,494 --> 00:11:44,800
And these people love us and there are more of them.

212
00:11:44,895 --> 00:11:48,240
Many people cheered on us online and didn't show up at the fancon.

213
00:11:48,539 --> 00:11:50,200
When I faced something bad,

214
00:11:50,363 --> 00:11:53,040
I'd remember that this small group didn't like us

215
00:11:53,182 --> 00:11:54,280
but these many people love us.

216
00:11:54,579 --> 00:11:55,992
We're good at this.

217
00:11:56,094 --> 00:12:00,080
Back to what you said that you were good at this, a year and a half ago,

218
00:12:00,184 --> 00:12:02,360
Orm, you told me that you barely praised yourself.

219
00:12:02,414 --> 00:12:05,240
- What? I said that? - You barely praised yourself out loud.

220
00:12:06,654 --> 00:12:07,760
You're right.

221
00:12:09,011 --> 00:12:12,761
The thought that I said earlier just came to me last night

222
00:12:12,802 --> 00:12:14,162
when I searched for the photo.

223
00:12:14,515 --> 00:12:17,000
The reason why I chose this one.

224
00:12:17,502 --> 00:12:21,160
I prepared the reason why I chose this photo.

225
00:12:21,200 --> 00:12:23,800
It was to remind me that 'I am that good, don’t ever forget that.'

226
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:28,200
It's nice. I just realized it now.

227
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,640
I just realized it now.

228
00:12:32,008 --> 00:12:34,009
- I'm happy for you. - Yeah.

229
00:12:34,126 --> 00:12:36,280
But your journey is still going.

230
00:12:36,327 --> 00:12:38,800
The reason that both of you visit me today

231
00:12:39,016 --> 00:12:41,300
is your journey to the third series.

232
00:12:41,331 --> 00:12:42,880
- That's right. - What is it called?

233
00:12:43,646 --> 00:12:47,315
(In unison) In Love Forever. (Wad Fun Wan Wiwa)

234
00:12:47,512 --> 00:12:50,080
How much are you growing when it's your third series already?

235
00:12:50,259 --> 00:12:52,640
We are working with Paa Jaew.

236
00:12:52,928 --> 00:12:56,680
Paa Jaew has a lot of knowledge to share.

237
00:12:58,160 --> 00:12:59,200
And I feel like

238
00:13:00,022 --> 00:13:02,480
I could use that knowledge.

239
00:13:03,728 --> 00:13:04,729
Yeah, I'm growing

240
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,078
a little bit.

241
00:13:07,744 --> 00:13:08,745
That's right.

242
00:13:09,105 --> 00:13:11,080
My role was

243
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,760
I mean I've never

244
00:13:15,064 --> 00:13:16,760
played this type of role before.

245
00:13:17,150 --> 00:13:20,420
My character gave me some perspective

246
00:13:21,384 --> 00:13:23,720
that is different from mine.

247
00:13:25,254 --> 00:13:29,200
The character gave me a chance to see the world differently.

248
00:13:30,528 --> 00:13:34,529
To see the world as it is, not romanticizing it.

249
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,920
- What about you, Orm? - I felt like this series…

250
00:13:38,038 --> 00:13:42,160
reflects the real life the most among the three series that I played with her.

251
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:45,840
What I meant was that like…

252
00:13:47,190 --> 00:13:50,240
the characters showed real emotions of love, jealousy, lust, greedy.

253
00:13:50,848 --> 00:13:53,680
And toxic, something like that. You know what I mean?

254
00:13:54,374 --> 00:13:56,981
In real life, you wanted to break up with someone and

255
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,160
you couldn't just walk away.

256
00:13:58,784 --> 00:14:02,640
It's a toxic relationship, trying to keep a relationship.

257
00:14:03,094 --> 00:14:06,120
I realized that love wasn't enough sometimes

258
00:14:07,208 --> 00:14:09,800
or something like that, it depended on various factors.

259
00:14:09,810 --> 00:14:13,520
I have a quick question, you two're in series together,

260
00:14:13,611 --> 00:14:15,480
from the first series until now,

261
00:14:15,736 --> 00:14:19,240
as viewers and they saw these ladies

262
00:14:19,464 --> 00:14:23,400
playing on screen, what are the vibes that they would get?

263
00:14:23,507 --> 00:14:26,608
I spent a lot of time on social media and I often saw

264
00:14:26,728 --> 00:14:31,400
our photos together and I thought 'why did she love me so much?'

265
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:35,440
It's true. I mean she loves me in real life.

266
00:14:35,950 --> 00:14:41,040
I get it now why the fans like to see us together.

267
00:14:41,720 --> 00:14:43,920
She takes good care of me.

268
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:46,760
Sometimes I didn't even see it

269
00:14:46,968 --> 00:14:50,720
and I saw it later in the clip. Like when I fell and she held me.

270
00:14:51,105 --> 00:14:55,800
When I was about to fall and she did this, something like that.

271
00:14:56,592 --> 00:14:58,600
She never said anything to me about it.

272
00:14:58,675 --> 00:15:02,160
I got from the last interview that Ling is a detail-oriented person.

273
00:15:02,176 --> 00:15:04,177
And I am the opposite.

274
00:15:05,893 --> 00:15:08,520
I think that this is the third series.

275
00:15:08,618 --> 00:15:10,360
And it is about…

276
00:15:11,310 --> 00:15:13,880
a life after your marriage.

277
00:15:14,184 --> 00:15:18,240
I think this is a great timing for me to portrait this role.

278
00:15:18,648 --> 00:15:24,040
If this series were our first, we wouldn't get this feeling.

279
00:15:24,216 --> 00:15:28,040
It wouldn't be as real as we were acting right now.

280
00:15:28,227 --> 00:15:32,440
- It's been two years that we worked together. - Spending life together.

281
00:15:32,451 --> 00:15:34,320
Just living, something like that.

282
00:15:35,374 --> 00:15:37,760
It is the right timing for it to be on the third series.

283
00:15:37,886 --> 00:15:41,520
We somehow shared

284
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:46,480
our closeness in real life in the series.

285
00:15:46,536 --> 00:15:50,520
- We portraited the characters… - Perfectly.

286
00:15:50,648 --> 00:15:55,170
You're promoting the series nonchalantly and I want to watch it now.

287
00:15:55,198 --> 00:15:57,720
I tried to do it discreetly.

288
00:15:57,800 --> 00:15:58,801
When is the premiere?

289
00:15:58,979 --> 00:16:01,800
- On 19th - of June.

290
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:08,000
The first episode was on already and people could watch it already.

291
00:16:08,760 --> 00:16:12,960
Tell me more about the series.

292
00:16:13,216 --> 00:16:16,280
I agreed that it was the right timing to air,

293
00:16:16,317 --> 00:16:19,720
when both of you got to know each other for a while.

294
00:16:20,120 --> 00:16:23,240
- I can't wait to watch it. - Kik also joined us.

295
00:16:23,478 --> 00:16:27,160
She is the best actress since I was born and met the actresses.

296
00:16:27,264 --> 00:16:31,280
It was fun when shooting with her. My neck hurt as well.

297
00:16:31,430 --> 00:16:34,920
She showed good facial expression, right? Her eye mucles?

298
00:16:34,966 --> 00:16:36,134
- It was so much fun. - Eye muscles?

299
00:16:36,480 --> 00:16:37,640
Eye muscles?

300
00:16:37,739 --> 00:16:40,520
You're right about her eye muscles.

301
00:16:40,576 --> 00:16:42,040
Using neck muscles as well.

302
00:16:42,512 --> 00:16:47,227
There was this scene that hurt my neck so bad, but it was so much fun.

303
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:48,608
They are waiting to watch the use of eye muscles right now.

304
00:16:48,742 --> 00:16:50,480
Eye muscles and neck muscles.

305
00:16:50,614 --> 00:16:54,680
I think the next photo should fit your life so well.

306
00:16:55,027 --> 00:16:57,028
And that is…

307
00:16:57,246 --> 00:16:58,744
the photo to reflect your safe space.

308
00:16:58,947 --> 00:17:01,680
What is Lingling Kwong's safe space?

309
00:17:02,043 --> 00:17:03,600
One..two…three.

310
00:17:07,046 --> 00:17:12,880
I went to Orm's graduation ceremony.

311
00:17:13,810 --> 00:17:15,319
I remember that day

312
00:17:15,762 --> 00:17:17,960
I was late before of bad traffic.

313
00:17:18,088 --> 00:17:21,440
I was in a van and I needed to switch to ride on a motorbike instead.

314
00:17:21,491 --> 00:17:23,300
It was the only way if I wanted to make it on time.

315
00:17:23,392 --> 00:17:26,880
I got it. It was a big event.

316
00:17:26,928 --> 00:17:33,360
It was a big event and it was my first time experiencing it.

317
00:17:33,760 --> 00:17:38,440
I felt like I wanted to congratulate

318
00:17:38,731 --> 00:17:41,480
her at that moment, I wanted to see…

319
00:17:41,611 --> 00:17:45,560
her hit another milestone.

320
00:17:45,936 --> 00:17:50,280
- I wanted to see her success. That's right. - Success.

321
00:17:50,300 --> 00:17:52,400
Her success in life, something like that.

322
00:17:52,904 --> 00:17:57,800
I saw this photo and the topic

323
00:17:58,126 --> 00:18:01,440
is my safe space and this is the one.

324
00:18:01,667 --> 00:18:03,520
What's on your mind when you rode that motorbike?

325
00:18:05,624 --> 00:18:08,200
- Oh my goodness, I was late. - It was late.

326
00:18:09,454 --> 00:18:14,040
- I was so nervous. - That day…

327
00:18:14,907 --> 00:18:18,560
- I swear I didn't know. - You didn't know, again.

328
00:18:18,678 --> 00:18:21,960
I didn't tell her.

329
00:18:22,176 --> 00:18:26,720
I knew that she really wanted me to come but I wanted to surprise her.

330
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:30,280
Did you expect that she would come?

331
00:18:30,401 --> 00:18:34,520
Not at all. I was afraid to ask people

332
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,882
- to come to my graduation. - But you asked me.

333
00:18:36,910 --> 00:18:38,911
- That's right. - She was afraid to ask. Still, she asked me.

334
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:43,000
When it was something about me, I would be shy.

335
00:18:43,118 --> 00:18:46,800
I would be so shy when I asked if they would come.

336
00:18:47,198 --> 00:18:50,187
She would be like 'Ling, will you come?'

337
00:18:50,199 --> 00:18:54,480
- I would ask her if she'd come on 17th? - Reenacting the real moment?

338
00:18:54,659 --> 00:18:57,680
- She asked me like this. - But if you're not free, then it's fine.

339
00:18:57,854 --> 00:18:59,040
Do you want to know her respond?

340
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:01,400
- I have work. - On 17th?

341
00:19:01,790 --> 00:19:04,960
I'm not sure, I think I have work.' I was like…

342
00:19:06,336 --> 00:19:07,337
It's fine.

343
00:19:07,494 --> 00:19:10,160
- I told her… - She pranked me.

344
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:14,216
She asked me twice.

345
00:19:14,344 --> 00:19:17,280
The first time I said that I wasn't sure.

346
00:19:17,395 --> 00:19:19,680
And the second time I said that I had work to do.

347
00:19:19,966 --> 00:19:21,040
I asked you twice?

348
00:19:21,195 --> 00:19:25,040
- You asked me twice, I remember. - She was mean to me.

349
00:19:25,131 --> 00:19:27,080
Deep down I felt like like this.

350
00:19:27,732 --> 00:19:30,040
- I lied to her. - That's right.

351
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:32,840
I made her believe that I wouldn't come for sure.

352
00:19:32,982 --> 00:19:37,600
I don't care much about who would show up on my special day.

353
00:19:37,920 --> 00:19:39,424
I can't even remember the birthdays.

354
00:19:39,467 --> 00:19:41,600
I don't even remember my own birthday or my friend's birthday.

355
00:19:41,702 --> 00:19:43,680
On the other hand, she hopped on a motorbike to be there.

356
00:19:43,936 --> 00:19:47,520
She didn't care much but she asked me twice.

357
00:19:48,110 --> 00:19:50,520
- I really don't care about it. - Hey, Orm.

358
00:19:50,579 --> 00:19:53,400
She becomes energetic now.

359
00:19:53,448 --> 00:19:56,320
- I wanted you there because we're close. - See? She wanted me there.

360
00:19:56,408 --> 00:20:00,000
I realized from the second time that she asked me

361
00:20:00,062 --> 00:20:02,800
Actually, you should have known from the first time.

362
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:07,720
I didn't have a clue. But I wasn't mad or anything.

363
00:20:07,730 --> 00:20:11,080
It was fine if she couldn't make it, I was just asking.

364
00:20:11,232 --> 00:20:12,233
I really mean it.

365
00:20:12,390 --> 00:20:17,360
Why is she your top safe-space person?

366
00:20:17,488 --> 00:20:21,224
I feel like working with

367
00:20:21,592 --> 00:20:26,560
a partner or anyone, I need to

368
00:20:26,771 --> 00:20:29,680
care for people that I work with.

369
00:20:29,752 --> 00:20:33,280
If she's not feeling well today,

370
00:20:33,619 --> 00:20:37,240
it's important that I care for her.

371
00:20:37,283 --> 00:20:39,480
She's been with me for such a long time.

372
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:44,880
Actually, I am not a kind of person who

373
00:20:44,915 --> 00:20:47,400
get an easy access to this, it takes time for me.

374
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:50,840
If you asked Orm about me,

375
00:20:50,862 --> 00:20:55,806
she would say that I wasn't that friendly.

376
00:20:55,998 --> 00:20:59,040
- She wasn't friendly. - I know.

377
00:20:59,843 --> 00:21:01,600
I'm not the type who would approach people first.

378
00:21:02,382 --> 00:21:04,040
It's not easy for me.

379
00:21:04,385 --> 00:21:09,118
I feel like we've been together for a long time

380
00:21:09,125 --> 00:21:12,200
and she gradually becomes my safe-space person.

381
00:21:12,515 --> 00:21:16,200
- People who can get through your wall… - That's right.

382
00:21:16,488 --> 00:21:20,600
I am a person who…

383
00:21:20,744 --> 00:21:24,100
- I am sincere to people around me. - That's true.

384
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:26,600
If I can give them something, I will do it right away.

385
00:21:27,096 --> 00:21:29,270
I am 100% sincere to my people.

386
00:21:29,403 --> 00:21:33,842
But it's hard to be that person for me.

387
00:21:34,262 --> 00:21:37,000
Let's see the picture from Orm.

388
00:21:37,243 --> 00:21:39,800
It is adorable as well, which is…

389
00:21:39,963 --> 00:21:42,400
Unichan.

390
00:21:42,470 --> 00:21:44,520
- Have you ever seen this one? - I haven't.

391
00:21:44,555 --> 00:21:46,100
We're in matching t-shirts.

392
00:21:46,139 --> 00:21:49,720
- Is this new or old photo? - The old one, see my blonde hair?

393
00:21:50,536 --> 00:21:52,400
It was since…

394
00:21:52,878 --> 00:21:55,280
Only You era?

395
00:21:55,736 --> 00:21:57,920
I think I just finished shooting the series.

396
00:21:57,955 --> 00:22:03,800
I still got my makeup on but my hair wasn't styled.

397
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:05,640
Why is your dog your safe space?

398
00:22:06,590 --> 00:22:09,160
So adorable.

399
00:22:09,432 --> 00:22:12,680
I feel like dogs

400
00:22:12,848 --> 00:22:14,800
loves us so much.

401
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:17,200
I heard people said that

402
00:22:18,283 --> 00:22:21,520
dogs are just a part of our life

403
00:22:21,899 --> 00:22:25,040
- but we are their whole life. - You're right.

404
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:29,239
Be strong.

405
00:22:29,542 --> 00:22:32,520
Yeah, like I said, my dog is my safe space because

406
00:22:32,595 --> 00:22:36,320
my dog can keep the best secret.

407
00:22:38,424 --> 00:22:39,800
My dog can never be mad at me.

408
00:22:41,182 --> 00:22:43,320
Unichan lives in my house,

409
00:22:43,843 --> 00:22:46,800
rarely leaves the house so I see my dog like my home.

410
00:22:47,315 --> 00:22:49,640
You know what I mean?

411
00:22:49,918 --> 00:22:53,520
My dog is my safe space because home is my safe space.

412
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:56,440
Now I know who I will talk to if I want to know your secret.

413
00:22:56,771 --> 00:23:00,280
That's right. Talk! I know you can talk.

414
00:23:00,456 --> 00:23:03,659
- Have you ever heard of the joke? From TikTok. - I have.

415
00:23:03,728 --> 00:23:05,480
Yeah, that's the story.

416
00:23:05,824 --> 00:23:09,147
If Uni could talk, Uni would know a lot of my secrets.

417
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:14,640
Orm, you said that it's not always nice or good about working.

418
00:23:14,918 --> 00:23:18,280
Sometimes you feel exhausted or couldn't take it anymore.

419
00:23:18,669 --> 00:23:22,200
When you couldn't take it anymore, or faced something tough,

420
00:23:22,597 --> 00:23:24,880
or have bad days.

421
00:23:25,931 --> 00:23:28,600
What did you say to yourself when you have one of these?

422
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:31,440
Did you let your guard down when you're around someone?

423
00:23:31,592 --> 00:23:33,500
Has anyone ever seen you when you're fragile?

424
00:23:33,779 --> 00:23:34,780
Not really.

425
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:36,840
You haven't shown it to anyone?

426
00:23:37,854 --> 00:23:41,760
I don't let things disturb me for so long.

427
00:23:42,454 --> 00:23:44,920
I don't normally cry to myself.

428
00:23:45,051 --> 00:23:49,264
I would be upset for a bit then I could let it go easily.

429
00:23:50,928 --> 00:23:53,880
I'm lucky that I'm so forgetful.

430
00:23:54,486 --> 00:23:57,280
- Ling, what about you? - Me?

431
00:23:57,960 --> 00:24:02,640
In the past one year and six months,

432
00:24:02,744 --> 00:24:07,400
I don't really have time for myself. I just got to be with myself

433
00:24:09,555 --> 00:24:11,280
when my new house finished.

434
00:24:12,758 --> 00:24:15,720
It was one of my goals that I told you

435
00:24:15,824 --> 00:24:18,280
- that I wanted to go home. - That's right.

436
00:24:18,360 --> 00:24:19,800
You told me that you wanted to go home.

437
00:24:20,462 --> 00:24:22,600
I wanted to go home in the country.

438
00:24:23,283 --> 00:24:28,680
On my day off, I sat down and I got to be with myself.

439
00:24:29,118 --> 00:24:33,400
I asked them for a few days off.

440
00:24:33,931 --> 00:24:36,642
And I felt like…

441
00:24:37,926 --> 00:24:42,640
I was in a room by myself.

442
00:24:43,590 --> 00:24:48,320
I thought about my life, what happened last year,

443
00:24:48,406 --> 00:24:49,880
what I faced last year.

444
00:24:50,246 --> 00:24:55,360
Referring to my earlier interview about myself,

445
00:24:56,880 --> 00:24:58,560
I felt like…

446
00:24:59,451 --> 00:25:02,560
it's a book that

447
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:04,561
I finished already.

448
00:25:05,912 --> 00:25:08,120
And I'm about to write a new book.

449
00:25:08,339 --> 00:25:12,600
It is a new version that I am still developing.

450
00:25:12,650 --> 00:25:15,080
I am looking for something new.

451
00:25:15,270 --> 00:25:18,920
I was done writing that book already.

452
00:25:19,024 --> 00:25:22,080
I am still looking and writing a new book.

453
00:25:23,176 --> 00:25:25,400
I felt like the past year

454
00:25:25,571 --> 00:25:29,880
there were good and bad things happened.

455
00:25:30,467 --> 00:25:33,720
There were something sad for me

456
00:25:34,895 --> 00:25:37,960
there were something that I wish I could have done it better.

457
00:25:38,992 --> 00:25:43,000
I reflected on my thoughts when I was at my new house.

458
00:25:43,918 --> 00:25:47,480
I had peaceful time to spend with myself.

459
00:25:48,440 --> 00:25:50,800
But nobody saw me like that.

460
00:25:52,589 --> 00:25:53,800
But you went through it already, right?

461
00:25:54,182 --> 00:25:57,200
- I think I'm still exploring it. - Understand.

462
00:25:57,376 --> 00:25:59,100
I'm still exploring.

463
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:01,800
What makes you happy?

464
00:26:02,475 --> 00:26:06,840
What brings smile to your face, both of you?

465
00:26:07,526 --> 00:26:09,527
My family and food.

466
00:26:10,560 --> 00:26:14,798
Dogs. I just see them and touch them

467
00:26:14,990 --> 00:26:18,400
and it brings smile to my face.

468
00:26:19,816 --> 00:26:21,817
When you think about your family,

469
00:26:21,900 --> 00:26:24,560
you'd think of a song 'Yesterday Once More.'

470
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:26,760
- Do you still listen to the song? - Sure, I do.

471
00:26:27,334 --> 00:26:30,400
Orm, if you need to write a letter to Lingling Kwong

472
00:26:30,474 --> 00:26:33,520
and give her encouragement, what would you write?

473
00:26:34,320 --> 00:26:35,480
Always be here.

474
00:26:38,200 --> 00:26:42,560
I always say it to people that are close to me that

475
00:26:43,288 --> 00:26:45,160
they can call me if something happens.

476
00:26:46,360 --> 00:26:51,000
I can talk to them for hours if they need me.

477
00:26:51,107 --> 00:26:54,240
they don't need to worry about their secrets leaking out.

478
00:26:54,250 --> 00:26:56,600
I'm serious about this. I'm a good listener.

479
00:26:56,760 --> 00:27:00,200
Perhaps I couldn't help them with their problems but

480
00:27:00,968 --> 00:27:04,920
I know that I am a good listener.

481
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:09,272
Or I'd ask if they want my perspective.

482
00:27:09,374 --> 00:27:12,480
I can help them with my perspective right away.

483
00:27:13,160 --> 00:27:16,161
I will be on my standby mode.

484
00:27:16,472 --> 00:27:19,040
I feel like there are a lot to talk to Lingling Kwong.

485
00:27:19,360 --> 00:27:23,160
- Really? - Yeah. It seems like you have a lot in your mind, Ling.

486
00:27:23,180 --> 00:27:27,480
I don't have a lot of friends.

487
00:27:28,379 --> 00:27:30,224
A few people know about what is going on in my life,

488
00:27:30,369 --> 00:27:32,011
and Ling is one of them.

489
00:27:33,307 --> 00:27:34,480
Ling knows a lot about me.

490
00:27:35,379 --> 00:27:36,920
You've been through a lot together, I think.

491
00:27:36,979 --> 00:27:39,840
We spent a lot of time together, I mean it's two years.

492
00:27:40,211 --> 00:27:43,120
We talked in all aspects, about our feelings.

493
00:27:44,056 --> 00:27:47,520
You know a lot about me. There's not much going on in my life.

494
00:27:47,784 --> 00:27:49,105
I don't have a lot of problems.

495
00:27:49,320 --> 00:27:50,720
Let's move on to the next photo.

496
00:27:51,032 --> 00:27:52,033
- Ling, are you okay? - I'm okay.

497
00:27:52,187 --> 00:27:56,520
- This is the one that people are most anticipated to see. - I sneaked up a little.

498
00:27:56,867 --> 00:28:00,760
Because it's the photo of each other that you took.

499
00:28:00,800 --> 00:28:02,355
The one that you like the most.

500
00:28:04,176 --> 00:28:05,680
One…two…three.

501
00:28:07,947 --> 00:28:09,920
- I've never seen this one before. - [The most adorable smile]

502
00:28:10,347 --> 00:28:14,840
I've never shown this one anywhere.

503
00:28:15,158 --> 00:28:19,000
I prepared a gift for Orm's birthday last year.

504
00:28:19,222 --> 00:28:22,440
I gave her a bird.

505
00:28:22,704 --> 00:28:27,320
She showed her brightest smile and she hugged..

506
00:28:27,798 --> 00:28:29,240
what is it called?

507
00:28:29,502 --> 00:28:31,880
A bird incubator.

508
00:28:31,918 --> 00:28:33,280
The bird's name is Abu.

509
00:28:33,571 --> 00:28:37,000
I felt like this was her happy moment.

510
00:28:37,606 --> 00:28:42,880
She smiled from her heart.

511
00:28:42,976 --> 00:28:44,592
Her genuine smile and it was the cutest.

512
00:28:44,662 --> 00:28:46,593
Among all of Orm's photos that you've taken,

513
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:49,240
why do you like this one the most?

514
00:28:49,574 --> 00:28:53,480
I think it is the cute smile of her.

515
00:28:54,256 --> 00:28:59,960
- And Orm never saw it before. - That's right.

516
00:29:00,328 --> 00:29:03,360
I didn't even realize when she took this pic of me.

517
00:29:03,406 --> 00:29:06,920
She must have paid attention to her new bird, that's why.

518
00:29:06,931 --> 00:29:08,320
It's possible, yeah.

519
00:29:08,355 --> 00:29:12,400
I carefully selected her birthday gift.

520
00:29:12,691 --> 00:29:18,040
I think the gift is a living animal that

521
00:29:19,040 --> 00:29:22,520
I spent such a long time to think about.

522
00:29:22,779 --> 00:29:26,400
It's an animal and needs to be responsible for.

523
00:29:26,500 --> 00:29:31,534
I know that Orm worked a lot.

524
00:29:31,625 --> 00:29:37,160
I think that giving her this will bright up her life.

525
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:41,840
This is the meaning behind this photo.

526
00:29:42,320 --> 00:29:46,000
You worked hard and you still smiled.

527
00:29:46,360 --> 00:29:51,960
There's no way that I worked hard and I would smile like that after.

528
00:29:53,080 --> 00:29:56,840
Normally, when she worked she would whine and want to go home.

529
00:29:57,032 --> 00:30:00,480
It would be her annoying face.

530
00:30:00,563 --> 00:30:03,680
The crew members are all laughing

531
00:30:03,715 --> 00:30:05,550
But this one…

532
00:30:06,184 --> 00:30:10,041
She looked so happy and lively in this photo.

533
00:30:10,392 --> 00:30:14,360
I've never felt so refreshing in my heart for such a long time.

534
00:30:14,854 --> 00:30:17,120
- True. She means it. - First time in years.

535
00:30:17,270 --> 00:30:20,280
From the first day that I worked until

536
00:30:20,368 --> 00:30:23,440
May of last year. I felt so happy.

537
00:30:23,808 --> 00:30:28,120
I ran to Abu and said hi.

538
00:30:29,043 --> 00:30:30,120
You know what I mean?

539
00:30:30,163 --> 00:30:32,200
- Abu made this sound. - It was the first day that you two met.

540
00:30:32,264 --> 00:30:36,800
I couldn't wait to bring Abu home.

541
00:30:37,080 --> 00:30:39,480
I wanted to show my dad, or something like that.

542
00:30:39,662 --> 00:30:44,560
I couldn't believe that she'd remember what I said.

543
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:45,761
I said it twice only.

544
00:30:46,440 --> 00:30:50,221
I told her that I wanted a bird and I asked her to choose the color.

545
00:30:50,227 --> 00:30:51,480
I think so.

546
00:30:52,520 --> 00:30:55,200
She listened to you but you had to say it twice.

547
00:30:55,235 --> 00:30:57,960
That's right. She always listens to me.

548
00:30:58,336 --> 00:31:01,040
It takes time for me. I need to be so sure.

549
00:31:01,248 --> 00:31:06,160
I'm worried that she would think that I wanted that stuff.

550
00:31:06,771 --> 00:31:10,840
I talked about birth twice and I was shocked that she remembered.

551
00:31:11,342 --> 00:31:13,230
Nobody surprised me with a gift like this.

552
00:31:15,907 --> 00:31:18,908
- Let's see Orm's version. - [Very professional]

553
00:31:20,776 --> 00:31:23,640
Can you tell us more about this photo? When did you take it?

554
00:31:24,675 --> 00:31:29,480
I think I played Fahlada, judging from location and my outfit.

555
00:31:29,624 --> 00:31:33,280
- I wrote 'very professional'. - Why's that?

556
00:31:33,502 --> 00:31:36,000
I don't see her face behind the camera.

557
00:31:36,104 --> 00:31:37,620
I feel like…

558
00:31:37,678 --> 00:31:40,449
- since we've been working together… - To focus.

559
00:31:40,568 --> 00:31:44,600
I think a person who operated it went to the bathroom.

560
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:48,240
So i went to see how it looked.

561
00:31:48,352 --> 00:31:50,000
- That's right. - And you didn't even know.

562
00:31:50,112 --> 00:31:52,760
It would take too long to look at the monitor.

563
00:31:52,928 --> 00:31:54,800
But she could look at it now

564
00:31:55,478 --> 00:31:58,700
I saw that she liked to look at this thing so much.

565
00:31:59,152 --> 00:32:01,400
I think it was a car accident scene.

566
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:07,001
No matter how rush it was for her to go home,

567
00:32:07,374 --> 00:32:10,400
- Ling still needed to check how she acted first. - That's right.

568
00:32:10,536 --> 00:32:13,920
She's a hard worker and I saw this picture and it was like…

569
00:32:13,987 --> 00:32:17,320
- I took it because she focused on her work. - It was the last scene.

570
00:32:17,862 --> 00:32:21,200
- It was the last scene, in front of the hospital. - If it was the last scene for me…

571
00:32:21,452 --> 00:32:24,453
I would go home as fast as I could, I wouldn't check the monitor.

572
00:32:24,460 --> 00:32:25,920
She wanted to go home.

573
00:32:26,208 --> 00:32:28,480
See? She still looked at the monitor.

574
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:32,120
- I remember it now. - I just snapped the picture.

575
00:32:32,840 --> 00:32:34,876
She focused on her work.

576
00:32:34,887 --> 00:32:38,800
She was so slim back then, so cute.

577
00:32:38,878 --> 00:32:40,720
I snapped her candid shot.

578
00:32:40,960 --> 00:32:44,240
I'd like to chat to you about your next photo.

579
00:32:44,451 --> 00:32:47,452
- The funny one? - Nope.

580
00:32:47,552 --> 00:32:49,880
My question is that…

581
00:32:50,360 --> 00:32:54,360
What if all of your photos were lost?

582
00:32:54,464 --> 00:32:57,920
But there was only one photo that you could restore.

583
00:32:58,000 --> 00:33:01,200
What photo would you like to restore?

584
00:33:01,694 --> 00:33:03,280
Which one is it?

585
00:33:03,640 --> 00:33:06,600
The answer is this one.

586
00:33:08,051 --> 00:33:12,240
I showed it already, it's our photo at Impact Arena.

587
00:33:13,187 --> 00:33:15,600
We took it with our 12,000 fans.

588
00:33:15,704 --> 00:33:18,160
- The second one ? - That's right.

589
00:33:18,238 --> 00:33:23,280
If I could only restore one photo back,

590
00:33:23,774 --> 00:33:28,725
I would get that one because it was the most valuable one to me.

591
00:33:30,747 --> 00:33:32,760
I must say that

592
00:33:32,960 --> 00:33:37,320
this kind of opportunity didn't just happen to anyone.

593
00:33:38,456 --> 00:33:41,240
I wasn't even born in Thailand.

594
00:33:41,939 --> 00:33:44,880
But I had a chance to perform at Impact Arena.

595
00:33:45,438 --> 00:33:49,600
I got to sing, to dance, to bring happiness to our fans.

596
00:33:50,860 --> 00:33:56,000
It was a meeting point of

597
00:33:56,632 --> 00:34:01,680
our fans from various places, even our international fans.

598
00:34:01,870 --> 00:34:04,880
It was a moment that

599
00:34:07,075 --> 00:34:09,639
very rare for me.

600
00:34:10,192 --> 00:34:12,971
This is from my opinion.

601
00:34:13,175 --> 00:34:16,000
I never thought that it would happen to me.

602
00:34:16,576 --> 00:34:19,368
This photo is special to me.

603
00:34:20,152 --> 00:34:24,520
I said on stage that I wanted to freeze this moment.

604
00:34:25,886 --> 00:34:28,520
I wanted to keep this moment forever.

605
00:34:28,525 --> 00:34:30,440
I could say that

606
00:34:32,219 --> 00:34:36,600
it was once-in-a-lifetime moment for me.

607
00:34:37,270 --> 00:34:39,281
I am not a singer.

608
00:34:40,100 --> 00:34:42,360
It was hard for me, I am not even a singer.

609
00:34:43,480 --> 00:34:46,320
That's why I chose this photo.

610
00:34:47,130 --> 00:34:49,859
If you get too exhausted, don't forget to look at these photos.

611
00:34:50,899 --> 00:34:53,400
Do you know what I'd do if I was so exhausted?

612
00:34:53,427 --> 00:34:54,560
Read letters from fans?

613
00:34:54,628 --> 00:34:56,520
I read letters from my fans.

614
00:34:57,043 --> 00:35:02,390
When I read their letters, it boost up my energy, every time.

615
00:35:02,774 --> 00:35:04,720
It gave me strength to go to work.

616
00:35:04,998 --> 00:35:07,800
It could be their best wishes to me.

617
00:35:07,910 --> 00:35:09,880
It could be their supportive messages,

618
00:35:09,915 --> 00:35:12,040
saying that I brought smiles to their faces.

619
00:35:12,104 --> 00:35:14,640
They shared their personal experiences through me.

620
00:35:15,048 --> 00:35:19,840
Many of them suffered from depression,

621
00:35:20,835 --> 00:35:25,320
or some of them weren't so confident, and they studied abroad.

622
00:35:25,902 --> 00:35:29,000
They had similar experiences like me.

623
00:35:29,576 --> 00:35:32,720
I want to be here to support them.

624
00:35:32,803 --> 00:35:34,320
If I can do it,

625
00:35:35,006 --> 00:35:36,720
anyone can do it.

626
00:35:37,486 --> 00:35:38,487
And I..

627
00:35:39,120 --> 00:35:44,950
want to inspire people, to encourage people, to my fans.

628
00:35:45,880 --> 00:35:47,160
And I feel…

629
00:35:49,392 --> 00:35:52,400
like I see more value in myself,

630
00:35:53,230 --> 00:35:54,800
just one more thing.

631
00:35:55,763 --> 00:35:57,700
You have your source of happiness,

632
00:35:58,803 --> 00:36:02,840
- from people's handwritings or emails. - That simple, from handwritings.

633
00:36:02,886 --> 00:36:04,560
They poured their hearts into writings.

634
00:36:04,848 --> 00:36:06,680
I saw some Chinese fans wrote in Thai.

635
00:36:06,811 --> 00:36:10,440
They studied Thai, to communicate with us.

636
00:36:12,560 --> 00:36:13,561
Excellent.

637
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:16,160
I can call your lives are phenomenal, both of you.

638
00:36:16,624 --> 00:36:18,680
It was phenomenal for sure.

639
00:36:19,360 --> 00:36:21,992
- Can I take a look at Orm's photo? - Sure.

640
00:36:22,078 --> 00:36:23,160
What is your photo?

641
00:36:23,341 --> 00:36:25,480
One…two…three.

642
00:36:25,939 --> 00:36:26,940
Yes, sir!'

643
00:36:27,840 --> 00:36:29,064
Can you tell us more about it?

644
00:36:29,384 --> 00:36:32,600
It is the football event.

645
00:36:33,611 --> 00:36:35,000
- Of Channel 3? - That's right.

646
00:36:35,462 --> 00:36:39,160
I chose this photo because I wanted the one that

647
00:36:41,835 --> 00:36:44,240
showed our activities with the fans.

648
00:36:44,875 --> 00:36:49,024
It was us who organized the event at Impact Arena.

649
00:36:49,323 --> 00:36:51,400
But this one was our fans organized it for us.

650
00:36:52,165 --> 00:36:54,560
Let's circle back to the moment that

651
00:36:55,531 --> 00:36:57,680
they are the most important people to us.

652
00:36:58,053 --> 00:37:02,899
I won't be where I am without them.

653
00:37:03,811 --> 00:37:07,400
I realized it lately

654
00:37:08,264 --> 00:37:11,320
especially when I felt burnt out,

655
00:37:11,582 --> 00:37:15,240
or I felt like I didn't want to do it anymore.

656
00:37:15,303 --> 00:37:18,000
Many times, we talked

657
00:37:18,718 --> 00:37:21,640
like I was so tired or I didn't want to wake up,

658
00:37:22,531 --> 00:37:24,840
this was what I talked to Ling.

659
00:37:25,774 --> 00:37:29,160
I had no motivation, I didn't know why I did this for.

660
00:37:29,304 --> 00:37:30,800
I'd think of this thing

661
00:37:31,878 --> 00:37:35,879
that many people are waiting to see us.

662
00:37:35,960 --> 00:37:37,280
Oh, it makes me emotional.

663
00:37:37,484 --> 00:37:39,160
I mean, I felt like

664
00:37:39,648 --> 00:37:43,300
if it wasn't for them, I wouldn't get up this morning.

665
00:37:43,960 --> 00:37:47,640
I would be rebel. Actually, I was…

666
00:37:49,336 --> 00:37:50,800
so attached to comfort in life.

667
00:37:50,837 --> 00:37:52,640
I didn't want to struggle in anything.

668
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:55,480
Eventually, I needed to step out of my comfort zone for the fans.

669
00:37:55,867 --> 00:37:58,920
If I have more projects to work on, if I play well in the series,

670
00:37:59,083 --> 00:38:01,682
they will see me in the projects and they will be so happy.

671
00:38:03,184 --> 00:38:04,840
I want to be at this position to be

672
00:38:06,366 --> 00:38:10,560
their light, lifeline or happiness.

673
00:38:11,167 --> 00:38:13,640
You know what I mean? Because I really feel that way.

674
00:38:13,741 --> 00:38:15,440
They are my motivation.

675
00:38:16,515 --> 00:38:19,480
Besides my family and people I love,

676
00:38:19,656 --> 00:38:21,960
I want to work for my fans.

677
00:38:22,109 --> 00:38:24,800
This is how I really feel from my heart.

678
00:38:25,640 --> 00:38:28,080
You said that you got emotional,

679
00:38:28,720 --> 00:38:32,320
I think people would cry in the comment section, many of them.

680
00:38:32,395 --> 00:38:34,520
- You think? - In YouTube, I can predict.

681
00:38:34,837 --> 00:38:36,640
It's true, it's really emotional for me.

682
00:38:36,832 --> 00:38:39,840
I woke up to work for them.

683
00:38:40,480 --> 00:38:42,880
My fans are my motivation, I always say that.

684
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:46,800
If you wouldn't get that kind of impact, you wouldn't feel this much.

685
00:38:46,939 --> 00:38:50,520
But you could feel it, whether in Thailand or overseas.

686
00:38:50,579 --> 00:38:51,280
You're right.

687
00:38:51,360 --> 00:38:53,281
Perhaps your most memorable day was when

688
00:38:53,361 --> 00:38:55,000
you were so exhausted and you met your fans.

689
00:38:55,891 --> 00:38:58,960
The great example is that I get homesick.

690
00:39:01,224 --> 00:39:02,760
When I travel for fanmeeting events,

691
00:39:03,144 --> 00:39:05,800
I cried all the time when I needed to travel abroad.

692
00:39:05,845 --> 00:39:08,400
I would cry to myself.

693
00:39:09,400 --> 00:39:12,520
I would cry for no reason.

694
00:39:12,734 --> 00:39:14,712
- Like I wanted to be in my own bed. - I see.

695
00:39:14,872 --> 00:39:19,440
If it was three-day event, I would be a little bit upset on my first day.

696
00:39:19,592 --> 00:39:21,920
The second day, I'd get so excited like it's about to be over soon.

697
00:39:21,944 --> 00:39:24,080
And I'd be so happy on the third day that I got to go home finally.

698
00:39:24,500 --> 00:39:28,040
I know that without the fans,

699
00:39:29,536 --> 00:39:31,280
it would be so sad and more upset, you know what I mean?

700
00:39:32,950 --> 00:39:34,440
I know that it will be many comments coming from your fans.

701
00:39:34,547 --> 00:39:37,920
Dear Myself is on YouTube for 10 months.

702
00:39:38,091 --> 00:39:41,280
People've requested LingOrm to my IG's DMs every week.

703
00:39:41,734 --> 00:39:44,440
They were asking when you two would be on the show again.

704
00:39:44,970 --> 00:39:46,440
I'm glad that we get to talk again today.

705
00:39:46,859 --> 00:39:48,200
I'm happy to be here, too.

706
00:39:48,672 --> 00:39:50,560
We're here at the last photo and it was too fast.

707
00:39:51,195 --> 00:39:52,880
- The last photo. - The last photo is the one that…

708
00:39:54,920 --> 00:39:58,600
reflects who you want to be in the next 10 years.

709
00:39:58,658 --> 00:40:00,880
Nobody took it for me. I took it myself.

710
00:40:00,926 --> 00:40:02,150
- You took it yourself? Really? - When was it?

711
00:40:02,302 --> 00:40:06,542
It was when I was in Cannes.

712
00:40:06,610 --> 00:40:08,880
I went with Dior Beauty.

713
00:40:09,246 --> 00:40:14,360
Actually, I went there to work and it was quite tough.

714
00:40:14,720 --> 00:40:17,920
Because we had a lot of photoshoots to finish.

715
00:40:18,552 --> 00:40:22,856
We finished up so late but I still got up early

716
00:40:22,947 --> 00:40:25,326
- for a morning run. - I see.

717
00:40:25,496 --> 00:40:29,960
I woke up early, opened the curtain and the weather was so nice.

718
00:40:30,179 --> 00:40:33,380
So I decided to run, to see the city.

719
00:40:34,136 --> 00:40:36,680
To see what the city looked like.

720
00:40:36,700 --> 00:40:39,640
I got to feel the city and see people.

721
00:40:41,120 --> 00:40:43,160
There was something that I rarely saw.

722
00:40:43,328 --> 00:40:49,482
Like I saw three people slept in sleeping bags by the beach.

723
00:40:49,520 --> 00:40:53,720
Or I saw someone who just got back from partying.

724
00:40:53,880 --> 00:40:56,280
They walked barefoot but they wore beautiful dresses.

725
00:40:56,800 --> 00:40:59,040
They were on their way back home, something like that.

726
00:41:00,300 --> 00:41:05,240
There were a lot for me to see and I enjoyed it.

727
00:41:05,470 --> 00:41:09,880
I feel like no matter how many years ahead,

728
00:41:10,071 --> 00:41:11,960
I still want to live my life

729
00:41:12,638 --> 00:41:17,000
that I have time for myself and enjoy my life,

730
00:41:17,582 --> 00:41:20,400
focusing on self-love, stay strong, stay healthy.

731
00:41:21,075 --> 00:41:25,840
It's the time for me to love myself and take care of myself.

732
00:41:27,142 --> 00:41:29,520
This is what the photo is about.

733
00:41:29,574 --> 00:41:33,680
After my morning run, I found a café and sat there by myself.

734
00:41:33,750 --> 00:41:37,000
I bought coffee and croissants for the team.

735
00:41:37,741 --> 00:41:40,320
You should teach how to take a good photo of ourselves like this.

736
00:41:40,419 --> 00:41:43,960
- So simple, just put your phone against croissant. - Are you serious?

737
00:41:44,086 --> 00:41:48,160
I didn't have a tripod with me, just my phone and my keycard

738
00:41:48,760 --> 00:41:51,120
when I went out to run. That's it.

739
00:41:51,403 --> 00:41:52,520
It is that simple.

740
00:41:52,651 --> 00:41:55,920
I saw that when you went overseas, you'd find time to run.

741
00:41:56,134 --> 00:41:59,640
If I have time,

742
00:41:59,835 --> 00:42:03,080
because it was rare for me.

743
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:05,356
No matter how tired I was,

744
00:42:05,576 --> 00:42:08,560
if I could still get up early with energy,

745
00:42:08,723 --> 00:42:11,160
I still wanted to go out to see people.

746
00:42:11,544 --> 00:42:12,545
to see…

747
00:42:13,278 --> 00:42:15,520
to enjoy weather and the city.

748
00:42:15,603 --> 00:42:17,123
It is another way to express love to yourself.

749
00:42:17,235 --> 00:42:19,880
That's right. It is my way to express love to myself.

750
00:42:20,744 --> 00:42:25,440
It was the moment that I got to leave everything behind.

751
00:42:26,675 --> 00:42:30,080
I didn't have to think and my head would be so clear.

752
00:42:30,894 --> 00:42:34,920
I just got to breathe and enjoyed the view along the road.

753
00:42:35,195 --> 00:42:40,240
Nobody cared that I ran by myself.

754
00:42:40,533 --> 00:42:43,600
I went for a run with her once. I was out of breath.

755
00:42:43,808 --> 00:42:46,280
She felt bad for me.

756
00:42:46,432 --> 00:42:48,800
She kept saying 'I'm sorry' to me.

757
00:42:48,854 --> 00:42:53,040
- Different speed. - I felt sorry for taking her for a run.

758
00:42:53,184 --> 00:42:56,200
- She was so exhausted. - That's good. You should do it more often.

759
00:42:56,678 --> 00:43:00,880
I like to run but I often meet with good runners.

760
00:43:01,206 --> 00:43:03,355
- They invited me to run with them. - I'm not good.

761
00:43:03,435 --> 00:43:08,360
Well, you exercise a lot.

762
00:43:08,935 --> 00:43:12,160
They are good at running and I was like this.

763
00:43:12,531 --> 00:43:14,400
I'm not good at running.

764
00:43:14,471 --> 00:43:17,760
- Baby steps first. - That's right, baby steps first.

765
00:43:18,400 --> 00:43:22,272
You can do it just by start doing it.

766
00:43:22,454 --> 00:43:24,760
- There is always first time in everything. - That's right.

767
00:43:24,827 --> 00:43:27,800
If you go with her the second time, then it is on you.

768
00:43:27,898 --> 00:43:30,240
Maybe next time. I'm kidding.

769
00:43:30,384 --> 00:43:32,480
The second time then what? You shouldn't.

770
00:43:32,645 --> 00:43:34,720
- No, the third time, I shouldn't. - What is the third time?

771
00:43:35,067 --> 00:43:36,184
What about the fouth time?

772
00:43:39,219 --> 00:43:42,280
- See that? She cracked a joke. - This is what Orm is.

773
00:43:42,320 --> 00:43:45,360
It shows who Ling is as well.

774
00:43:46,331 --> 00:43:49,160
Let's take a look at Orm's photo.

775
00:43:49,302 --> 00:43:50,960
Let's see what you want to be in 10 years.

776
00:43:52,758 --> 00:43:55,240
- You want to go back to study? - Nope.

777
00:43:55,300 --> 00:43:57,600
I don't think so. You shouldn't ask it the second time.

778
00:43:57,758 --> 00:43:58,759
Got it.

779
00:43:58,859 --> 00:44:02,320
I wanted to show a photo of my family.

780
00:44:02,472 --> 00:44:04,473
Because I wanted to see your reflection

781
00:44:04,503 --> 00:44:06,040
- of yourself in the next 10 years. - That's right.

782
00:44:08,160 --> 00:44:11,120
I want to be with my family.

783
00:44:12,086 --> 00:44:15,120
I want to live my life

784
00:44:15,971 --> 00:44:18,520
with my family, great family.

785
00:44:19,779 --> 00:44:20,780
And…

786
00:44:21,822 --> 00:44:23,600
I can do whatever I want to.

787
00:44:24,094 --> 00:44:26,095
I want to keep growing.

788
00:44:27,200 --> 00:44:28,760
I still want this job.

789
00:44:29,275 --> 00:44:33,600
I love this job, love people who support me.

790
00:44:35,451 --> 00:44:36,720
Yeah.

791
00:44:37,300 --> 00:44:39,160
I want to start a family.

792
00:44:39,934 --> 00:44:42,880
I want to live peacefully and not disturb anybody.

793
00:44:42,979 --> 00:44:45,181
I'm not surprised you chose this one

794
00:44:45,200 --> 00:44:47,464
because you've always said that your family is your BFF.

795
00:44:47,725 --> 00:44:49,080
That's right.

796
00:44:49,437 --> 00:44:53,120
My family always has been my BFF until now.

797
00:44:53,656 --> 00:44:56,520
- And your mom is here with you. - That's right. She's here.

798
00:44:56,657 --> 00:44:58,547
- She's not listening. - Her mom is…

799
00:44:59,203 --> 00:45:03,960
always with her. She goes to every country with Orm.

800
00:45:04,339 --> 00:45:08,400
She will follow and take care of Orm.

801
00:45:09,600 --> 00:45:11,601
This is the first time in one and a half years that I got to talk to you.

802
00:45:11,651 --> 00:45:15,280
I have one question that I ask all of my guests.

803
00:45:15,385 --> 00:45:18,720
What do you want to say to yourself?

804
00:45:18,837 --> 00:45:20,838
After our conservation from the first photo,

805
00:45:21,099 --> 00:45:24,560
a photo of you two together for the first time,

806
00:45:24,741 --> 00:45:28,862
we talked about your journey, your safe space,

807
00:45:29,022 --> 00:45:30,339
your lost photos that you wish to restore,

808
00:45:30,664 --> 00:45:34,800
what do you want to say to yourself today?

809
00:45:35,507 --> 00:45:36,508
What is the message?

810
00:45:36,672 --> 00:45:37,960
I want to say that…

811
00:45:39,450 --> 00:45:41,280
life goes on.

812
00:45:41,830 --> 00:45:45,760
Therefore, you need to stay strong like this,

813
00:45:46,670 --> 00:45:47,880
and become even stronger.

814
00:45:50,478 --> 00:45:54,640
You need to move on and march forward.

815
00:45:58,120 --> 00:45:59,121
Keep growing.

816
00:46:00,643 --> 00:46:02,120
This is what I want to say to myself.

817
00:46:02,520 --> 00:46:05,360
- What about you, Lingling Kwong? - Me?

818
00:46:05,960 --> 00:46:07,720
Ling Kwong…

819
00:46:08,470 --> 00:46:09,880
Don't be scared.

820
00:46:15,125 --> 00:46:16,560
And…

821
00:46:22,048 --> 00:46:24,480
keep on walking no matter what you will face.

822
00:46:26,438 --> 00:46:27,744
Your past could be good or bad,

823
00:46:28,747 --> 00:46:31,520
in the future, there are many more new things for you to try,

824
00:46:32,634 --> 00:46:37,707
so don't get intimidated.

825
00:46:38,544 --> 00:46:41,520
Whatever you will face, keep on going.

826
00:46:41,744 --> 00:46:42,745
You're right.

827
00:46:43,771 --> 00:46:44,960
Don't give up.

828
00:46:45,872 --> 00:46:48,280
The most important question,

829
00:46:48,710 --> 00:46:50,040
a little bit of cliché though,

830
00:46:50,182 --> 00:46:53,800
people that will be on this journey with you

831
00:46:54,187 --> 00:46:56,080
are Ling and Orm.

832
00:46:56,363 --> 00:47:01,200
What do you want to say to a person next to you?

833
00:47:02,230 --> 00:47:03,640
I want to tell Ling that…

834
00:47:05,520 --> 00:47:06,521
you're the best.

835
00:47:07,008 --> 00:47:08,920
This is the first one that I'm going to say to you.

836
00:47:09,275 --> 00:47:10,960
I feel like she is

837
00:47:11,787 --> 00:47:15,360
so talented and I hope you stay this way forever.

838
00:47:15,659 --> 00:47:16,660
Thank you.

839
00:47:16,848 --> 00:47:19,600
Which leads to the next one that I'd like to say to you,

840
00:47:19,649 --> 00:47:22,760
I wish you a lot of happiness,

841
00:47:23,560 --> 00:47:25,100
I wish you can do things that you want to.

842
00:47:25,523 --> 00:47:26,760
Thank you.

843
00:47:28,126 --> 00:47:31,080
Last time, she wrote you a letter and she asked

844
00:47:31,371 --> 00:47:34,240
if you completed the lists of what you want to do. Do you remember?

845
00:47:34,549 --> 00:47:37,200
- I do. - You need to ask yourself.

846
00:47:37,355 --> 00:47:39,120
Do you get a chance to do what you want?

847
00:47:39,739 --> 00:47:43,560
- There are many things that I want to do. - I can't wait to see them.

848
00:47:44,267 --> 00:47:48,400
I completed some of them already.

849
00:47:49,200 --> 00:47:52,440
I'm happy and I'm proud of myself.

850
00:47:52,819 --> 00:47:54,163
Lastly, what do you want to say to her?

851
00:47:55,480 --> 00:47:58,600
To Orm? I want to give her a round of applause.

852
00:48:00,576 --> 00:48:05,760
In the past one year and six months,

853
00:48:05,814 --> 00:48:07,320
you're so great.

854
00:48:07,990 --> 00:48:11,200
I feel like you have been growing up a lot.

855
00:48:11,630 --> 00:48:14,000
And you are doing better.

856
00:48:14,067 --> 00:48:18,000
When you faced some dramas and you dealt with them better.

857
00:48:18,068 --> 00:48:19,760
- You need to praise yourself a lot more. - Okay.

858
00:48:20,091 --> 00:48:24,840
And I wish that you…

859
00:48:25,958 --> 00:48:29,040
don't have to feel like you're getting chubby, just eat.

860
00:48:29,270 --> 00:48:32,160
- Yeah, please eat. - Am I good or what?

861
00:48:32,200 --> 00:48:33,700
I feel like…

862
00:48:34,830 --> 00:48:38,900
Orm is taking a better care of herself.

863
00:48:39,880 --> 00:48:43,120
She started to work out instead of eating less.

864
00:48:43,579 --> 00:48:46,000
I told her that it wasn't good for her health.

865
00:48:46,502 --> 00:48:48,960
And she never listened to me.

866
00:48:49,131 --> 00:48:54,400
Lately, she started to work out.

867
00:48:54,432 --> 00:48:59,667
I appreciated that she started to work out and just keep going.

868
00:49:00,222 --> 00:49:05,400
I wish her to follow her dream and do what she loves.

869
00:49:05,971 --> 00:49:06,972
Thank you.

870
00:49:07,139 --> 00:49:11,440
We will be watching your lives and your success as well.

871
00:49:12,075 --> 00:49:15,680
Thank you Lingling and Orm for visiting Dear Myself,

872
00:49:15,702 --> 00:49:17,480
I know that you're working so hard and so exhausted.

873
00:49:17,734 --> 00:49:20,320
I think encouragement from me wouldn't be enough.

874
00:49:20,558 --> 00:49:24,800
Our viewers, please leave your comments for our guests.

875
00:49:25,096 --> 00:49:29,011
I'm sure that you all support them and watch their journey.

876
00:49:29,406 --> 00:49:32,560
Good luck on your third series, and fourth, fifth and more.

877
00:49:32,736 --> 00:49:35,600
- Thank you. - Thank you.

878
00:49:35,984 --> 00:49:36,985
I'll talk to you later.

879
00:49:37,120 --> 00:49:39,840
- Talk to you later. - I'm glad to talk to you.

880
00:49:39,921 --> 00:49:44,440
I was so excited to join the show and look up the photos.

881
00:49:44,811 --> 00:49:47,480
- Thank you for inviting us here. - Thank you for coming.

882
00:49:47,542 --> 00:49:50,040
- Thank you. - It's been a year and a half.

883
00:49:50,214 --> 00:49:54,520
Thank you for watching Ling and Orm until now.

884
00:49:54,752 --> 00:49:57,240
Please give them lots of support, I'm sure you do.

885
00:49:57,318 --> 00:49:58,440
But please give them more of your support.

886
00:49:58,507 --> 00:50:02,000
Don't forget to like, share and subscribe to Praew Magazine,

887
00:50:02,040 --> 00:50:05,480
so you won't miss our next Dear Myself's guests.

888
00:50:05,643 --> 00:50:08,392
Thank you for Filobula for furniture on set.

889
00:50:08,470 --> 00:50:10,080
Thank you lights and lamps from Lamptitude

890
00:50:10,100 --> 00:50:11,760
Thank you Livingstyle for tree decorations.

891
00:50:11,779 --> 00:50:14,760
We're recording at Praew Studio in One Bangkok.

892
00:50:14,958 --> 00:50:16,840
Stay tuned to see who our next guest is.

893
00:50:16,915 --> 00:50:18,680
We should let our guests take a break.

894
00:50:18,846 --> 00:50:21,000
See you later, Lingling and Orm.

895
00:50:21,059 --> 00:50:25,280
- Thank you, thank you so much. Bye. - Thank you and bye.

896
00:50:26,510 --> 00:50:28,440
Life goes on.

897
00:50:28,984 --> 00:50:32,880
Therefore, you need to stay strong like this,

898
00:50:33,655 --> 00:50:38,600
Don't dwell on how good or bad your past is.

899
00:50:39,790 --> 00:50:43,360
In the end, there are many great things

900
00:50:43,584 --> 00:50:45,000
waiting for you in the future.

901
00:50:47,301 --> 00:50:48,720
No matter what you will be facing,

902
00:50:49,400 --> 00:50:51,120
- you need to keep going. - That's right.

903
00:50:52,520 --> 00:50:53,521
Don't give up.